            <chunk name="Object" index="15">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6335e941-00a5-4562-99da-f1d8120f8cb9</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">INDOOR CO2 + OCCUPANCY
Two CO2 paths on one canvas. Units: METERS.

CFD PATH (top): room 6 x 4 x 3 m, inlet 1 m2 at
0.5 m/s on x=0, outlet on x=6, cell size 0.3 m.
CO2 Emitter zone box (4,1,1)-(5,3,2), injection
rate 1.076e-4. Solves on the incompressible
solver: CO2 is a passive scalar, not buoyant.
Numbers from TestIndoorEmittersContainerE2E.

ANALYTIC PATH (bottom): Occupant CO2 at age 25,
1.2 met, sex average -&gt; 0.0043 L/s, the Persily
&amp; de Jonge row pinned in TestIndoorAirQuality.
CO2 Air Quality grades 950 ppm against 400 ppm
outdoor on EN 16798-1 -&gt; delta 550 -&gt; Category I,
the exact boundary the unit test pins.

KNOWN WARNING: Indoor Case reports the emitter
zone is 1 m at its thinnest against the 1.2 m
background cell (4 x cell size). That is the
fixture's own zone; the fixture asserts the zone
does select cells after snappy refinement. Lower
Cell Size if you widen the room.

Occupant count is not an input on either CO2
component - see Window Air Exchange for that.

Action toggles ship OFF.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
